file.content:
[
  {
    "id": "c001",
    "name": "D. Additional Provisions",
    "text": "D. ADDITIONAL PROVISIONS Licensee will pay $1400.00 monthly for use of the ARP Protocols and consultation. This fee will be automatically debited from the below listed credit card or checking account."
  },
  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "Equipment Lease Grant",
    "text": "ARP WAVE CLINIC EQUIPMENT LEASE ARP WAVE, LLC, a Minnesota Limited Liability Company (\"hereinafter called Lessor\") whose address is 451 Cliff Road East, Suite 106, Burnsville, MN 55337, hereby leases to the Clinic Operator, (hereinafter called \"Lessee\") and Lessee hereby hires and leases from Lessor, the equipment and machinery described above, referred to herein as \"equipment,\" upon the following terms and conditions."
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "1. Term",
    "text": "1, Term, The term of this Lease with respects to the equipment leased hereunder shall begin with the first day of the month following the date of shipment or delivery and shall continue in full force and effect for the period of months indicated in Block A above, said period hereinafter referred to as the “original term\". ONE YEAR"
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "Rent",
    "text": "Rent. Lessee shall pay to Lessor as rental for the equipment leased hereunder, the sum shown in Block B above during the original term, said rental to be paid in advance or before the first day of each month during the original term, to Lessor at its above designated office or at such other place and/or to such other person as Lessor may from time to time designate in writing. EQUIPMENT $68,250.00 PROTOCOLS $16,800.00"
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "Selection of Equipment, Additional Equipment and Inspection",
    "text": "Selection of Equipment, Additional Equipment and Inspection. Lessee has requested equipment of the type and quantity specified above and has selected the supplier named above. Lessee and Lessor agree that this Lease is a \"True Lease\" as defined by the Uniform Commercial Code Article 2A, the Uniform Personal Property Leasing Act. Lessor shall not be liable for specific performance of this Lease or for damages if for any reason the supplier delays or fails to fill the order for the equipment. Lessee shall accept such equipment if delivered in good repair, and hereby authorizes Lessor to add to this Lease the serial number of each item of equipment so delivered. Any delay in such delivery shall not affect the validity of this Lease. The Lessee shall inspect the equipment within forty-eight (48) hours after receipt thereof. Unless the Lessee within said period of time gives written notice to the Lessor specifying any defect in or other proper objection to the equipment, the Lessee agrees that it shall be conclusively presumed as between Lessor and Lessee, that Lessee has fully inspected, has acknowledged that the equipment is in good condition and repair and that the Lessee has found the equipment acceptable to it under the terms of the Lease. Unless the Lessor receives notice as provided by this paragraph, the term of this Lease shall begin and payment shall be due to Lessor as provided by Paragraph 1 of this Lease."
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "Additional Equipment",
    "text": "ADDITIONAL EQUIPMENT CAN BE LEASED BY EXECUTING AN ADDENDUM TO THIS AGREEMENT THAT DESCRIBES THE NEW EQUIPMENT, THE RENTAL RATE AND LEASE TERM,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c007",
    "name": "Warranty",
    "text": "Warranty. Lessor shall repair defects to the equipment free of charge during the term of this lease so long as the defect does not arise out misuse or negligence on the part of Lessee. If required repair is determined to be the result of misuse or negligence on the part of Lessee, then Lessee shall be responsible for payment of all costs incurred in making the repair. If a repair is required, Lessee shall ship the equipment to Lessor’s facility for inspection and repair as necessary."
  },
  {
    "id": "c008",
    "name": "Disclaimer of Warranty",
    "text": "Disclaimer of Warranty. EXCEPT AS IS SPECIFICALLY PROVIDED HEREIN, LESSOR MAKES NO EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTY AS TO ANY MATTER WHATSOEVER, INCLUDING, WITHOUT LIMITATION, THE DESIGN OR CONDITION OF EQUIPMENT, ITS MERCHANTABILITY OR ITS FITNESS FOR ANY PARTICULAR PURPOSE, THE QUALITY OF MATERIAL OR WORKMANSHIP OF THE EQUIPMENT OR ITS CONFORMITY WITH ANY SPECIFICATIONS OR ORDER; NO DEFECT OR UNFITNESS OF THE EQUIPMENT SHALL RELIEVE LESSEE OF THE OBLIGATION UNDER THIS LEASE,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c009",
    "name": "Liability of Lessor",
    "text": "Liability of Lessor, LESSOR AND THE PARTY FROM WHOM LESSOR LEASES THE EQUIPMENT IN THE EVENT THE EQUIPMENT IS NOT OWNED BY LESSOR, SHALL NOT BE LIABLE TO LESSEE, OR TO ANY OTHER PERSON, FIRM, OR CORPORATION, FOR ANY LOSS OR INTERRUPTION OF OR DAMAGE TO BUSINESS, OR PROFITS, OR FOR ANY OTHER DAMAGES OF ANY KIND OR NATURE WHATSOEVER, DIRECT OR CONSEQUENTIAL, RESULTING FROM THE DELAY OR FAILURE TO FURNISH EQUIPMENT HEREUNDER, OR THE FAILURE OF THE EQUIPMENT TO OPERATE OR FAULTY OPERATION OF THE EQUIPMENT OR SYSTEM, OR IN ANY MANNER RESULTING FROM THE INSTALLATON, OPERATION, SERVICE OR USE OF THE EQUIPMENT LEASED HEREUNDER. THE LESSOR’S LIABILITY TO THE LESSEE, IF ANY, SHALL IN NO EVENT EXCEED THE TOTAL AMOUNT OF RENT PAID BY THE LESSEE TO THE LESSOR UNDER THE LEASE AT THE TIME THE CLAIM IS MADE,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c010",
    "name": "Ownership and Alterations of Equipment",
    "text": "Ownership and Alterations of Equipment. The equipment shall at all times be and remain, the sole and exclusive property of the Lessor and the Lessee shall have no right, title or interest therein or thereto except as expressly set forth in this Lease. Without the prior written consent of the Lessor, the Lessee shall not make any alterations, changes, additions or improvements to the equipment, All additions and improvements of whatsoever kind or nature made to the equipment shall belong to and become the property of Lessor upon the expiration or earlier termination of this lease,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c011",
    "name": "Loss and Damage; Maintenance",
    "text": "Loss and Damage; Maintenance The Lessee hereby assumes and shall bear the entire risk of loss and damage to the equipment from any and every cause whatsoever. No loss or damage to the equipment or any part thereof shall impair any obligation of the Lessee under this Lease which shall continue in full force and effect, including but not limited to the obligations of the Lessee to make rental payments, except as provided in this Paragraph 13. If the equipment is determined by Lessor, in its sole discretion, to be repairable, Lessee shall be liable to repair the equipment at its expense and to continue making rental payments as provided by this Lease. Lessee shall keep the A.R.P Trainers in good repair and any repair shall be at the Lessee’s cost. There shall be no modification of the A.R.P. Trainers."
  },
  {
    "id": "c012",
    "name": "Lessee's Obligations Unconditional",
    "text": "Lessee's Obligations Unconditional, Lessee’s obligations to pay all rent, and all the rights of Lessor in and to such payments, shall be absolute and unconditional and shall not be subject to any abatement, reduction, set-off, defense, counter claim or recoupment for any reason, including without limitation, any such amount due or alleged to be due, to, or by reason of, any past, present or future claims which Lessee may have against Lessor, the manufacturer or any other seller of the equipment, or any other person or entity, for any reason, Except as otherwise expressly provided herein, this Lease shall not terminate nor shall the respective obligations of the Lessor or the Lessee be affected, by reason of defect in or casualty to or obsolescence of the equipment from any cause, or by the interference with the use thereof by any private person, corporation or governmental authority or any other disability of the Lessee to use the equipment, or for any other cause, whether similar or dissimilar to the foregoing, including, but not limited to, war, act of god, governmental regulations, any present or future law or regulation to the contrary not withstanding, It is the express intention of the Lessor and Lessee that all rent payable by the Lessee hereunder shall be, and continued to be, payable in all events unless the obligation to pay the same shall be terminated pursuant to the express provisions of this Lease."
  },
  {
    "id": "c013",
    "name": "Insurance",
    "text": "The Lessee shall keep the equipment insured against all risks of loss or damage from every cause whatsoever for not less than the full replacement value thereof as determined by the Lessor; and shall carry public liability and property damage insurance covering the equipment. All said insurance shall be in form and amount and with companies approved by the Lessor, and shall be in the joint names of the Lessor and the Lessee."
  },
  {
    "id": "c014",
    "name": "Encumbrances, Taxes, and Fees",
    "text": "Encumbrances, Taxes, and Fees, Lessee shall keep the equipment leased hereunder free from all liens, security interests and encumbrances of any nature whatsoever, and shall pay all license fees, registration fees, assessments, charges and taxes which may now or hereafter be imposed by any governmental authority upon the leasing, renting, sale, possession, use or ownership of the equipment, excluding all taxes on or measured by Lessor's income."
  },
  {
    "id": "c015",
    "name": "10. Surrender",
    "text": "10. Surrender. Upon the expiration or earlier termination of this Lease, with respect to any item of equipment, the Lessee shall return the same to the Lessor in good repair, condition and working order, ordinary wear and tear resulting from proper use thereof alone excepted, in the following manner as may be specified by the Lessor: a, By delivering such item of equipment at the Lessee's cost and expense to such place as the Lessor shall specify within the county in which the same was delivered to the Lessee or to which same was moved with the written consent of the Lessor; or, b. By loading such item of equipment at the Lessee's cost and expense on board such carrier as the Lessor shall specify and shipping the same, freight prepaid, to the destination, within the continental United States, designated by the Lessor,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c016",
    "name": "11. Default",
    "text": "11. Default. If Lessee shall be in default under any conditions of this Agreement; if Lessee shall be in default or in breach under any conditions of the License Agreement or any other agreement executed with ARP WAVE; if Lessee shall file a voluntary petition in bankruptcy or shall make an assignment for the benefit of creditors or shall be adjudicated a bankrupt; if there is a dissolution, whether voluntary or involuntary, or other termination of the existence of Lessee; if any representation or warranty, or any document or instrument furnished to the Lessee in connection with the transaction proves to be false in any material respect or omits to state any material fact; if any individual guarantor of the Lease should die, become insolvent, or file for protection under any bankruptcy or similar law; or if Lessor deems itself insecure, Lessor shall have the right to exercise any one or more of the following remedies: a. To declare the entire amount of rent hereunder immediately due and payable as to any or all items of equipment, without notice or demand to the Lessee. b. To sue for and recover all rents, and other payments, then accrued or thereafter accruing, with respect to all items of equipment. _ @ To take possession of any or all items of equipment without demand or notice, wherever the same shall be located, without any court order or other process of law. The Lessee hereby waives any and all damage occasioned by such taking of possession. Any said taking of possession shall not constitute a termination of this Lease as to any or all items of equipment uniess the Lessor expressly so notifies the Lessee in writing, d. To terminate this Lease as to any or all items of equipment. e. To pursue any other remedy at law or in equity. Notwithstanding any said repossession or any other action which the Lessor may take, the Lessee shall be and remain liable for performance of all obligations on its part to be performed under this Lease. Lessee hereby waives any and all damages occasioned by the exercise by Lessor of any of Lessor's rights or remedies upon the occurrence of an event of default under this section, Lessee agrees to indemnify Lessor for all costs and expenses, including reasonable attorneys’ fees, incurred by the Lessor in connection with the enforcement by it of any of its rights or remedies under the Lease. Any default under the License Agreement or any other agreement signed contemporaneously between Lessor and Lessee shall be deemed a to be a default under this Lease Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c017",
    "name": "12. Indemnity",
    "text": "12, Indemnity. The Lessee shall indemnify the Lessor against, and hold the Lessor harmless from, any and all claims, actions, suits, proceedings, costs, expenses, damages, and liabilities, including attorney's fees, arising out of, connected with, or resulting from the equipment, including without limiting the generality of the foregoing, the manufacture, selection, delivery, possession, use, operation or return of the equipment. It is expressly understood that it is possible by acting outside the scope of use, the equipment can in the manner of its use cause harm to the applicator and the applicatee. As such the Licensee shall follow at all times the protocols licensed in conjunction with the equipment under a separate agreement and never use the equipment on a person with a pacemaker,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c018",
    "name": "13. Assignment",
    "text": "13. Assignment, Without the prior written consent of the Lessor, the Lessee shall not (a) assign, transfer, pledge or hypothecate this Lease, the equipment or any part thereof, or any interest therein or (b) sublet or lend the equipment or any part thereof, or permit the equipment or any part thereof to be used by anyone other than the Lessee or the Lessee's employees. Consent to any of the foregoing prohibited acts applies only in the given instance, and is not a consent to any subsequent like act by the Lessee or any other person, Subject always to the foregoing, this Lease inures to the benefit of, and is binding upon, the heirs, legatees, personal representatives, successors and assigns of the parties hereto,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c019",
    "name": "14. Lessor's Assignment",
    "text": "14, Lessor's Assignment. All rights of the Lessor hereunder may be assigned, pledged, mortgaged, transferred or otherwise disposed of, either in whole or in part, without notice to the Lessee, If the Lessor assigns this Lease or the rentals due or to become due hereunder or any other interest herein whether as security for any of its indebtedness or otherwise, no breach or default by the Lessor hereunder or pursuant to any other agreement between the Lessor or the Lessee, if any, shall excuse performance by the Lessee of any provision hereof. No such assignee shall be obligated to perform any duly, covenant or condition required to be performed by the Lessor under the terms of this Lease,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c020",
    "name": "16. Interest",
    "text": "16, Interest. Should the Lessee fail to pay any portion of the rent herein reserved or any other sum required by the Lessee to be paid to the Lessor within ten (10) days after the due date hereof, the Lessee shall pay unto the Lessor interest on such delinquent payment from the expiration of said ten (10) days until paid at the highest rate permitted by the laws of the state whose laws govern this Agreement, but not to exceed 8% per annum."
  },
  {
    "id": "c021",
    "name": "17. Offset",
    "text": "17. Offset. The Lessee hereby waives any and all existing and future claims and offsets against any rent or other payments due hereunder; and agrees to pay the rent and other amounts hereunder regardless of any offset or claims which may be asserted by the Lessee or on its behalf. Lessor is authorized by Lessee to apply or cause to be applied against amounts owing Lessor hereunder any amounts which might from time to time be owed to Lessor or any affiliate of Lessor by Lessee,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c022",
    "name": "18. Entire Agreement",
    "text": "18, Entire Agreement. 19, 20. 21. This Lease constitutes the entire agreement between the parties hereto; and this Lease shall not be modified, amended, altered, or changed except by a written agreement signed by the parties hereto."
  },
  {
    "id": "c023",
    "name": "19. Multiple Lessees",
    "text": "Multiple Lessees, If there is more than one Lessee named in this Lease, the liability of each shall be joint and several."
  },
  {
    "id": "c024",
    "name": "20. Non-Waiver",
    "text": "Non-Waiver. Neither the failure of either party to insist upon the performance of any term or condition of this Lease or to exercise any right or privilege conferred by this Lease nor the waiver by either party of any such term or condition shall be construed as thereafter waiving any such term, condition, right or privilege."
  },
  {
    "id": "c025",
    "name": "Section 21 — Forum Selection (Equipment Lease)",
    "text": "Venue for the enforcement of this Agreement shall be limited to the Hennepin County, Minnesota, Federal or State District Court to the exclusion of all other courts, but subject to appeal as provided for under Minnesota law and applicable rules of civil and appellate procedure."
  },
  {
    "id": "c026",
    "name": "22. Notice",
    "text": "22, Notice. All notices, requests and other communications required or permitted to be given hereunder shall be in writing and shall be deemed to have been duly given if delivered personally, given by prepaid telegram or mailed first class, postage prepaid, registered or certified mail, to the address listed hereon for the Lessor and Lessee, or to such other address as either party shall notify the other, by the means described in this paragraph."
  },
  {
    "id": "c027",
    "name": "23. Severability",
    "text": "23. Severability. If any provision of the Lease is held to be unenforceable, the remainder of the Lease shall not be affected thereby but shall remain valid and enforceable. If any provision of this Lease is so broad as to be unenforceable, such provision shall be sufficiently narrowed so as to make it enforceable."
  },
  {
    "id": "c028",
    "name": "License Agreement Parties",
    "text": "ARP WAVE CLINIC LICENSE AGREEMENT THIS AGREEMENT is made on the date appearing below, by and between ARP WAVE, LLC, a Minnesota Limited Liability Company with its principal place of business at 451 Cliff Road East, Suite 106, Burnsville, MN 55337 (hereinafter sometimes referred to as “ARP” or “Licensor’”) and (sometimes hereinafter referred to as “Licensee”),"
  },
  {
    "id": "c029",
    "name": "Licensor Ownership Recital",
    "text": "WHEREAS, Licensor is the owner of all right, title and interest in and to ARP Wave™, Accelerated Recovery Program Protocols, Ultra Fit Athletic Mastery Protocols and In Balance Muscle Testing Protocols, related programs, and related intellectual property (hereinafter sometimes referred to collectively and/or independently as “System(s)y”), and this property is being licensed to Licensee under the terms and conditions set forth below;"
  },
  {
    "id": "c030",
    "name": "License Intent Recital",
    "text": "WHEREAS, Licensee has indicated to Licensor a desire to have a non-exclusive license for the use of said System(s)s set forth in Section 2 below in an ARP Wave Clinic, subject to the terms of this Agreement and to Licensor’s ongoing monitoring, revision, upgrading, customizing, updating and modification as Licensor may deem necessary or appropriate in its sole and absolute discretion;"
  },
  {
    "id": "c031",
    "name": "Section 1.1—System(s)",
    "text": "SECTION 1 — DEFINITIONS I, “System(s)” shall mean the Licensor’s proprietary training protocols and programs, copyrights, trade marks, service marks, trade secrets and all other intellectual property associated with Accelerated Recovery Program Protocols, Ultra Fit Athletic Mastery Protocols and In Balance Muscle Testing Protocols, related programs, and related intellectual property, The System(s), and any and all rights thereto, shall at all times remain the exclusive intellectual and material property of Licensor."
  },
  {
    "id": "c032",
    "name": "Section 1.2—ARP Wave Clinic",
    "text": "2. “ARP Wave Clinic” shall mean a facility operating for the purpose of providing rehabilitative and physical training services to the public by use of the Systems described herein and pursuant to the terms and covenants of this Lease/License Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c033",
    "name": "Section 1.3—ARP Trademarks",
    "text": "3, \"ARP Trademarks\" means all names, marks, logos, designs, trade dress and other brand designations used by ARP Wave, LLC in connection with its products and services. In performing its obligations hereunder, Licensee may refer to the Systems by the associated ARP Trademarks, provided that such reference is not misleading and complies with any guidelines issued by ARP Wave. Licensee is granted no right, title or license to, or interest in, any ARP Trademarks. Licensee acknowledges and agrees that any use of the ARP Trademarks by Licensee will inure to the sole benefit of ARP Wave. If Licensee acquires any rights in any ARP Trademarks by operation of law or otherwise, it will immediately, at no cost or expense to ARP, assign such rights to ARP along with all associated goodwill."
  },
  {
    "id": "c034",
    "name": "Section 2.1—License Grant",
    "text": "SECTION 2 ~ LICENSE Ll. ARP Wave leases to Lessee/Licensee the equipment described above (as more specifically set forth in the equipment lease), In addition, ARP Wave grants to Licensee a limited non-exclusive, nontransferable license for use of the following System(s): Accelerated Recovery Performance Protocols In Balance Muscle Testing Protocols Wave Site Protocols solely in accordance with the terms and conditions set forth in this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c035",
    "name": "Section 2.2—Clinic Name Right",
    "text": "2. During the term of this License, Licensee shall have the non-exclusive revocable right to operate its clinic facility under the business name of “ARP Wave Clinic” for as long as the Licensee fully complies and is not in breach of this or any other agreements with ARP Wave, LLC."
  },
  {
    "id": "c036",
    "name": "Section 2.3—Nontransferability",
    "text": "3, Licensor and Licensee acknowledge and agree that Licensees rights herein are not transferable and are forfeitable in the event of certain circumstances or occurrences as herein set forth, At no time shall the rights of Licensee herein, or any portion thereof, either voluntarily or involuntarily, be further assigned, transferred, conveyed or otherwise disposed of by Licensee, Any such attempted conveyance or transfer shall be deemed a breach of this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c037",
    "name": "Section 2.4—Enhancements and Modifications",
    "text": "4. Licensee acknowledges and agrees that without Licensor’s express written consent, Licensee shall not make enhancements or modify, or alter the System(s) or any parts thereof, herein provided and licensed to Licensee, and that, moreover, regardless if said consent is obtained, any further enhancements of said System(s) or any parts thereof, shall at all times remain the sole and absolutely property of Licensor. Licensee and Licensor agree that from time to time Licensor may make enhancements or otherwise modify or alter the System(s) provided and licensed herein and that all such enhancements shall be the property of Licensor and the use thereof will be governed by this License,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c038",
    "name": "Section 2.5—Assignment and Sublicensing",
    "text": "5. Without limitation to anything aforesaid, there shall be no right of assignment or sublicense provided to Licensee under this Agreement. Licensor, however, shall at any time be entitled to assign this Agreement, in whole or in part, without the prior written consent of Licensee, to such person, entity, trust or other third party as Licensor may in its sole and absolute discretion determine. In the event of such assignment, provided Licensee is afforded notice of such assignment by Licensor, this Licensor shall then have no responsibility or liability or any continued obligations of any nature whatsoever to Licensee herein."
  },
  {
    "id": "c039",
    "name": "Section 3—Maintenance and Support",
    "text": "SECTION 3 ~ MAINTENANCE AND SUPPORT Licensor shall provide the following support to Licensee: Monthly seminars in Minneapolis, Minnesota, Telephone Consultation and Email Support. On site support can be provided to Licensee for an additional fee of $1500.00 per day plus all expenses for each team member traveling."
  },
  {
    "id": "c040",
    "name": "Section 4.1—Clinic Personnel and Services",
    "text": "SECTION 4 —- LICENSEE’S RESPONSIBILITY/CONFIDENTIALITY/NON-COMPETE. 1. In order to initiate and maintain an ARP Wave Clinic, Licensee must have trained medical personnel on site daily in the form of either a DC, DO, MD, PT. An ARP Wave Clinic must exclusively use the Systems licensed hereunder for provision of its services to the public and must not perform any other type of physical therapy, training or rehabilitative service during the term of this license agreement. An ARP Wave Clinic must maintain trained therapy personnel in the Systems licensed pursuant to this agreement. Licensee must insure that its trained therapy personnel participate in continuing education related to all of the Systems license hereunder which will be provided by the Licensor."
  },
  {
    "id": "c041",
    "name": "Section 4.2—Personnel Training and Costs",
    "text": "2, Licensee shall be responsible for training all of its personnel who promote the Systems or ARP Wave Clinic so that they are knowledgeable about the Systems and can adequately represent the ARP Wave Clinic. All costs, including salaries, commissions, bonuses, contributions to social security or other welfare system payments, benefits, severance pay and other expenses incurred by Licensee in connection with its performance of this Agreement or the operation of ARP Wave Clinic shall be borne solely by Licensee."
  },
  {
    "id": "c042",
    "name": "Section 4.3—Professional Conduct",
    "text": "3. Licensee will at all times perform hereunder in a professional manner and in accordance with this Agreement and any reasonable guidelines issued by ARP Wave. Licensee will: (a) conduct business in a manner that reflects favorably at all times on the Licensee and the good name, goodwill and reputation of ARP Wave; (b) avoid deceptive, misleading or unethical practices that are or might be detrimental to ARP Wave, the Licensee or the public, including but not limited to disparagement of ARP Wave or the Licensee; (c) make no false or misleading representation with respect to ARP Wave or the Licensee; and (d) make no representations with respect to ARP Wave or the Licensee that are inconsistent with ARP Wave’s lease and license agreement for the Licensee, promotional materials and other literature distributed by ARP Wave, including all liability limitations and disclaimers contained in such materials."
  },
  {
    "id": "c043",
    "name": "Section 4.4—Permits, Compliance and Patient Data",
    "text": "4, Licensee will, at its sole cost and expense, obtain all permits and licenses necessary in connection with its performance of this Agreement, and will comply with all applicable laws, rules and regulations in the performance of this Agreement. Licensee will at all times during the term of this Agreement maintain appropriate technical and organizational measures to protect any patient data that it collects, accesses or processes in connection with this Agreement against unauthorized or unlawful use, disclosure, processing or alteration. Licensee will act in all instances in accordance with all applicable laws, rules and regulations in relation to the collection, use, disclosure and processing of any patient data."
  },
  {
    "id": "c044",
    "name": "Section 4.5—Proprietary Rights and Confidentiality",
    "text": "5, Without limitation, the trademarks and service marks which are part of the System(s), are owned exclusively by the Licensor. Licensee acknowledges and agrees that the System(s) herein licensed are proprietary to Licensor and constitute trade marks, service marks, copyrights and trade secrets of Licensor, and title thereto is not conveyed to Licensee and that Licensee’s sole right and interest in and to the System(s) is the License herein granted, Without limiting anything else herein set forth, Licensee shall not sell, transfer, publish, disclose, display ot otherwise make available the System(s) to any other patty without the written consent of Licensor. The provisions of this paragraph shall not be deemed to derogate or lessen responsibilities set forth in any other provision hereof or available at law."
  },
  {
    "id": "c045",
    "name": "Section 4.6—Non-Compete",
    "text": "6. Licensee and its officers, affiliate companies, employees, agents and representatives agree not to license, lease, sell, manufacture, or otherwise represent any similar or competitive system or Licensee within the Territory defined in the Exclusive Licensee Agreement executed by the parties, for the duration of this Agreement and then for a period of Two (2) years beyond the termination of this Agreement for whatever reason,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c046",
    "name": "Section 5—Fees",
    "text": "SECTION 5 ~ FEES Licensee shall pay the Licensor as license fees hereunder the sum of $1400.00 a month."
  },
  {
    "id": "c047",
    "name": "Section 6.1—Term",
    "text": "SECTION 6 ~- TERM AND TERMINATION 1, This Agreement shall become effective on and shall be continue in full force and effect until unless otherwise terminated by Licensor pursuant to the terms of this agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c048",
    "name": "Section 6.2—Survival",
    "text": "2, When and in the event this Agreement is terminated, the covenants and provisions herein set forth shall survive such termination, except those covenants as pertaining to future payments to be made by Licensee,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c049",
    "name": "Section 6.3—Automatic Termination",
    "text": "3. This license shall be deemed automatically terminated or revoked: (i) in the event of a judgment, levy, lien, attachment, notice of foreclosure, or other adverse creditor action against Licensee pertaining to the R possession, ownership or operation of said right to use said System(s); (ii) any Licensee attempt to hypothecate, pledge, sell, transfer, sublicense, assign or convey, whether voluntary or involuntary, this license right."
  },
  {
    "id": "c050",
    "name": "Section 7.1—Default and Remedies",
